 "lesson": [
  {
   "id": "scg-b01",
   "type": "text",
   "md": "# Graphs of sine and cosine\n\nAs $t$ travels around the unit circle, the $y$-coordinate of $P(t)$ rises and falls between $-1$ and $1$. Plot that height against $t$ and you get the **sine wave**; plot the $x$-coordinate and you get the **cosine wave**. Both repeat every $2\\pi$."
  },
