  {
   "id": "scg-b06",
   "type": "callout",
   "kind": "definition",
   "title": "Period, range and symmetry",
   "md": "Both functions have **period** $2\\pi$ and **range** $[-1,1]$. Sine is **odd**, so its graph is symmetric about the origin; cosine is **even**, so its graph is symmetric about the $y$-axis."
  },
  {
   "id": "scg-b07",
   "type": "example",
   "title": "Sketch $y=-\\sin x$",
   "problem": "Sketch one period of $y=-\\sin x$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "md": "Start from the key points of $\\sin x$: $(0,0)$, $(\\frac{\\pi}{2},1)$, $(\\pi,0)$, $(\\frac{3\\pi}{2},-1)$, $(2\\pi,0)$."
    },
    {
     "md": "Multiply every $y$ by $-1$: $(0,0)$, $(\\frac{\\pi}{2},-1)$, $(\\pi,0)$, $(\\frac{3\\pi}{2},1)$, $(2\\pi,0)$."
    },
    {
     "md": "Join them with a smooth wave: it goes **down** first."
    }
   ],
   "answer": "A sine wave reflected over the $x$-axis."
  },
